<urn:atm:triage:finding/WINCLIPPY-003-AL8>
  a triage:Finding ;
  triage:findingId "WINCLIPPY-003-AL8" ;
  triage:title "atm-daemon-bootstrap Windows-only clippy unused-import dead-code (NonZeroU32, HOST_RUNTIME_SOCKET_FILE)" ;
  triage:description "On PR #778 (feature/pal-s8-daemon-composition-proof, head 8500375f694b688f05976823545338d1998b1d4c, post WINCLIPPY-002-AL8 fix), the 'Just lint (windows-latest)' CI job still fails clippy in crate atm-daemon-bootstrap: unused import 'NonZeroU32' (crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/lib.rs:7, 'use std::num::{NonZeroU32, NonZeroUsize};') and unused import 'HOST_RUNTIME_SOCKET_FILE' (crates/atm-daemon-bootstrap/src/lib.rs:15, 'use atm_core::home::{HOST_RUNTIME_SOCKET_FILE, current_host_runtime_scope};'). Root cause: both symbols are only consumed inside 'unix_socket_config_for_uid' (lib.rs:169-181), which is reached only via the '#[cfg(unix)]'-gated 'unix_socket_config' (lib.rs:154-165); the non-unix stub 'unix_socket_config' (lib.rs:187+) does not reference either symbol, so on Windows both imports are unused. quality-mgr confirmed via git blame that both imports predate WINCLIPPY-001-AL8 and WINCLIPPY-002-AL8 entirely—they were introduced in base AL.8 commit f28ee24e ('feat(AL.8): activate Tokio Axum daemon composition'). This was masked until now because atm-daemon-bootstrap depends on atm-http-runtime, so windows-latest clippy never got past the atm-http-runtime errors (WINCLIPPY-001-AL8, WINCLIPPY-002-AL8) far enough to reach this crate's own diagnostics. This is a pre-existing latent defect surfaced now, not a regression introduced by the WINCLIPPY-001/002-AL8 fix rounds." ;
  triage:phaseId "phase-al" ;
  triage:triageMode "initial_pass" ;
  triage:category "portability-lint" ;
  triage:severity "blocking" ;
  triage:repeatable true ;
  triage:sweepScope "crate" ;
